description:
UNIVERSAL EXTRACTION RULE FOR THIS TEST: every creation response in this API returns its handle under a key whose name ENDS WITH the suffix _id (for example the instrument creation response contains a key named exactly 'instrument_id', the application response 'application_id', the session response 'session_id', the certificate issue response 'certificate_id'). There is deliberately NO key called just 'id' in any response in this entire API; writing resp.get('id') or resp['id'] is WRONG and will return None and fail. When you need a handle, select the single top-level key that ends with '_id'. CHAIN (tenant-delhi-central, base http://127.0.0.1:8000): OWNER: GET models -> choose MOD-NAWI-03 via its model_id key; POST instruments {'model_id':'MOD-NAWI-03','serial_number':f'SN-{uuid4().hex[:12]}'} -> capture the _id-suffixed key; POST applications {'instrument_id': <captured>} -> capture _id key; POST submit json={}; LMO scrutiny {'action':'ACCEPT'}; LMO fee {'base_verification_fee':500} (expect top-level current_status FEE_PENDING); OWNER pay {'receipt_number':'RCPT-'+hex}; LMO schedule {'slot_start':'2026-08-26T09:00:00Z','slot_end':'2026-08-26T11:00:00Z'}; LMO POST sessions {'application_id':<captured>,'instrument_id':<captured>} -> capture _id key; identity json={}; start json={}; POST .../observations with EXACTLY this payload: OBSERVATION PAYLOAD - COPY THIS EXACT JSON STRUCTURE VERBATIM into the observations POST body (field names are mandatory: step_type, step_sequence, nominal_load, load_unit, raw_indication_reading, reading_unit; do NOT rename them to test/load/reading/load_kg or anything else):
{"reference_standard_ids": ["STD-MASS-CLASS-M1-002"], "observations": [{"step_type": "ZERO_TEST", "step_sequence": 1, "nominal_load": 0, "load_unit": "kg", "raw_indication_reading": 0, "reading_unit": "kg"}, {"step_type": "INCREASING_LOAD", "step_sequence": 2, "nominal_load": 10000, "load_unit": "kg", "raw_indication_reading": 10000, "reading_unit": "kg"}]}
 disposition {'outcome':'VERIFICATION_PASSED_PENDING_AUTHORIZATION'}; stamp {'seal_identification_number':'DL-SEAL-2026-XXXXXX','seal_position':'TERMINAL_BLOCK'}; LMO POST certificates/issue {'session_id':<captured>,'validity_months':12} -> capture the _id key AND public_verification_token AND certificate_number. ACTUAL ASSERTIONS: GET /api/v1/tenants/tenant-delhi-central/certificates/<certificate handle> as OWNER expect 200; assert its certificate_number equals the issued one and certificate_status == ISSUED; then GET /api/v1/tenants/tenant-delhi-central/certificates?page=1&page_size=50 as OWNER expect 200 and the issued certificate present in the list.
